From: Cong Nguyen <cong.nguyen.zn@renesas.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] srvcore: Do not log an error when the SoC timer clock is not
 configured

PVRSRVGetSocFreqKM() is called by user space every time a client connects
to the GPU (timestamp correlation for PVRScope/profiling). It logs

    PVR_K:(Error): NNN: SOC Timer is not configured correctly [1058]

whenever RGX_TIMING_INFORMATION::ui32SOCClockSpeed is 0. The R-Car system
layer (services/system/rgx_rcar/sysconfig.c) never fills that field and the
build does not enable SUPPORT_SOC_TIMER, so on R-Car V4H every GL/Vulkan
client produces one of these lines in dmesg although nothing is wrong: the
value is only reported back to user space, the driver does not depend on it.

Log it as an informational message instead (off by default, visible with
PVRDebugLevel), so dmesg is not flooded and real PVR_K errors stand out.
---
 rogue_km/services/server/common/srvcore.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/rogue_km/services/server/common/srvcore.c
+++ b/rogue_km/services/server/common/srvcore.c
@@ -1053,9 +1053,13 @@ PVRSRV_ERROR PVRSRVGetSocFreqKM(CONNECTION_DATA *psConnection,
 	RGX_DATA *psRGXData = (RGX_DATA*)psDeviceNode->psDevConfig->hDevData;
 	PVR_UNREFERENCED_PARAMETER(psConnection);
 
+	/* System layers that do not drive the SoC timer (e.g. R-Car: no
+	 * SUPPORT_SOC_TIMER, ui32SOCClockSpeed left at 0) hit this on every
+	 * client connection; it is informational only, do not spam dmesg. */
 	if (psRGXData->psRGXTimingInfo->ui32SOCClockSpeed == 0)
 	{
-		PVR_DPF((PVR_DBG_ERROR, "SOC Timer is not configured correctly"));
+		PVR_DPF((PVR_DBG_MESSAGE, "%s: SOC timer clock speed not configured "
+		         "by the system layer (reporting 0)", __func__));
 	}
 
 	*pui32SocFreq = psRGXData->psRGXTimingInfo->ui32SOCClockSpeed;
